    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c4926ea2_353d8a24",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/GlobalCache.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-10T02:04:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I originally chose to make it public (and guarded by the spin lock) because I wasn\u0027t sure if there would end up being utility in being able to stash a resource in the global cache later on as you\u0027re using the context. That\u0027s also why I typed it as Resource instead of just for Buffers.\n\nBut if that\u0027s the case there ought to be a matching way to remove a Resource from static resources or we could get ourselves in trouble with leaks, and we don\u0027t want to have too many permanent resources anyways so it makes sense to restrict who can actual add resources. If we restrict it to just StaticBufferManager then you\u0027re right that we don\u0027t need to guard its access because it will always be single threaded before the Context is returned. That said, keeping it guarded won\u0027t hurt performance in this case and makes it obvious GlobalCache remains thread safe, since we don\u0027t have a great way to assert when addStaticResource() is called that we\u0027re still in the initialization phase.",
      "parentUuid": "0bff0cdc_ddc74b02",
